<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donika Kastrioti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1506</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Andronika Arianiti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Donika Kastrioti, born Andronika Arianiti, was the daughter of the Albanian nobleman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjergj-arianiti">Gjergj Arianiti</a> and the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>, whom she married in 1451. The marriage bound the powerful Arianiti family to Skanderbeg's cause. After his death in 1468 she left Albania with their son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjon-kastrioti">Gjon Kastrioti</a> II for the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, where she lived until her death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/donika-kastrioti.jpg" alt="Donika Kastrioti" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodoor de Bry · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Donika_Kastrioti_engraving.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
